<h2>Country comparison</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Germany</strong> — automotive and industrial demand; the largest established market, with local cell and pack capacity under construction.</li>
<li><strong>France</strong> — policy-led gigafactory build-out; demand is strong but local supply is still scaling.</li>
<li><strong>UK</strong> — import-heavy, with automotive demand and a developing local capacity story.</li>
<li><strong>EU regulation</strong> — applies across the single market and changes the documentation and end-of-life cost for every country.</li>
</ul>
<h2>What to verify</h2>
<p>Ask for the carbon-footprint declaration, the recycled-content statement and the battery-passport data model before comparing prices. A supplier that cannot provide them is not aligned with the direction of the regulation, even if the product is technically acceptable today.</p>
